{"id":"SMA-425","title":"Add paigasus.common.v1.AuditMetadata + per-language Auditable interface","description":"Define a single source-of-truth shape for audit fields on auditable entities and DTOs — `created_at`, `modified_at`, `created_by`, `modified_by` — defined once in proto (ADR-0004) and generated into Rust / Python / TypeScript, with a thin, idiomatic `Auditable` interface layered on the generated type per language.

This lands the first real `paigasus.common.v1` contract (the package was scaffolded empty in <issue id="2651acfc-55de-45c6-9976-fede71901b0a" href="https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-360/bootstrap-contracts-proto-workspace-with-buf-scaffold">SMA-360</issue>, placeholder removed in <issue id="f945ac67-abd7-446b-9be4-42529f6e5a14" href="https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-389/wire-paigasus-proto-build-contractsgenerate-dependency-edges-when">SMA-389</issue>).

## Design decisions (resolved)

* **Defined in proto, not Rust.** Audit fields are a *data shape* that crosses the language boundary, so the single definition lives in `contracts/` and buf fans it out (ADR-0004). The `paigasus-kernel` → FFI path (ADR-0005) is for *behavior* and is the wrong tool here — PyO3/napi expose functions, and a Rust trait does not transit FFI as an "interface" in Py/TS.
* **Embedded message, not flat fields.** Carry the metadata by embedding `AuditMetadata` as a field (`AuditMetadata audit = N;`) rather than repeating four fields per message. Proto3 has no inheritance/mixins, so embedding is how "defined once" is actually achieved.
* `google.protobuf.Timestamp` for the two timestamps (well-known type; ships with buf, no new buf dep — note it is *not* part of the existing googleapis dep).
* **Opaque** `string` for `created_by` / `modified_by` (user id / subject claim / service name). Empty string = unknown/system, pending a future structured `Actor` type.
* `_at` **field naming.** Timestamp fields use the protobuf-idiomatic `created_at` / `modified_at`. Settled before regen — renaming after generated code lands is a breaking change to the wire contract.
* **"Interface" = thin per-language wrapper.** The generated message gives the shape in all three languages; the programmable `Auditable` contract is a few idiomatic lines per language (Rust `trait`, TS `interface`, Python `Protocol`) over the generated type — no logic reimplemented, consistent with ADR-0005.

## Proposed proto

`contracts/proto/paigasus/common/v1/audit.proto`

```proto
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
syntax = "proto3";

package paigasus.common.v1;

import "google/protobuf/timestamp.proto";

// Shared audit metadata for auditable entities and DTOs across all Paigasus
// services and languages. Carried by *embedding* this message as a field
// (`AuditMetadata audit = N;`) rather than repeating the four fields per
// message — the shape is defined once here. The per-language `Auditable`
// trait / interface / Protocol is layered on top of the generated type.
message AuditMetadata {
  // When the entity was first created (UTC).
  google.protobuf.Timestamp created_at = 1;

  // When the entity was last modified (UTC). Equals created_at on first write.
  google.protobuf.Timestamp modified_at = 2;

  // Opaque identifier of the actor that created the entity (user id / subject
  // claim / service name). Empty = unknown/system, pending a structured Actor.
  string created_by = 3;

  // Opaque identifier of the actor that last modified the entity.
  string modified_by = 4;
}
```

Usage on a DTO (illustrative):

```proto
message Widget {
  string id = 1;
  // ... domain fields ...
  paigasus.common.v1.AuditMetadata audit = 15;
}
```

## Proposed per-language thin interfaces

These are **hand-written and must live OUTSIDE the** `generated/` **dirs** — `buf.gen.yaml` sets `clean: true`, which wipes each `out:` dir on every regen.

**Rust** — `rs/crates/libs/paigasus-proto/src/audit.rs`

```rust
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
use crate::paigasus::common::v1::AuditMetadata;

/// Implemented by any DTO/entity that carries [`AuditMetadata`].
pub trait Auditable {
    /// The embedded audit metadata, if present.
    fn audit(&self) -> Option<&AuditMetadata>;

    fn created_by(&self) -> Option<&str> {
        self.audit().map(|a| a.created_by.as_str())
    }
    fn modified_by(&self) -> Option<&str> {
        self.audit().map(|a| a.modified_by.as_str())
    }
    fn created_at(&self) -> Option<&::prost_types::Timestamp> {
        self.audit().and_then(|a| a.created_at.as_ref())
    }
    fn modified_at(&self) -> Option<&::prost_types::Timestamp> {
        self.audit().and_then(|a| a.modified_at.as_ref())
    }
}
```

Wiring: add a generated `common::v1` module include + `pub mod audit;` to `paigasus-proto/src/lib.rs`, and add a `prost-types` dependency (prost maps `google.protobuf.Timestamp` → `::prost_types::Timestamp` because `compile_well_known_types` is set only on the tonic plugin, not prost). `prost-types = "0.14"` should be added to `rs/Cargo.toml [workspace.dependencies]` to track the pinned prost 0.14.

**TypeScript** — `ts/packages/paigasus-proto/src/audit.ts`

```ts
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
import type { AuditMetadata } from "./generated/paigasus/common/v1/audit_pb.js";

/** Structural interface satisfied by any generated message embedding AuditMetadata. */
export interface Auditable {
  audit?: AuditMetadata;
}
```

protobuf-es generates message-typed fields as optional, and TS is structurally typed, so any generated DTO with `audit?: AuditMetadata` satisfies `Auditable` for free. Re-export from `src/index.ts`.

**Python** — `py/packages/paigasus-proto/src/paigasus_proto/audit.py`

```python
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
from typing import Protocol, runtime_checkable

from .generated.paigasus.common.v1 import AuditMetadata


@runtime_checkable
class Auditable(Protocol):
    audit: "AuditMetadata | None"
```

betterproto2 embeds the message as `audit: "AuditMetadata | None"`; the structural `Protocol` matches any such DTO.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `contracts/proto/paigasus/common/v1/audit.proto` added as above with `created_at` / `modified_at`; `moon run contracts:lint` and `buf format --exit-code` pass.
- [ ] `moon run contracts:generate` produces `AuditMetadata` in all three targets; generated code committed (ADR-0004).
- [ ] Rust: `audit.rs` trait + `lib.rs` wiring for `common::v1`; `prost-types` added (workspace dep + `paigasus-proto`); `cargo build --workspace` and `cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings` clean; a unit test impls `Auditable` on a throwaway DTO embedding `AuditMetadata`.
- [ ] TS: `audit.ts` interface + `index.ts` re-export; `tsc --noEmit` clean; a vitest test asserts a created message structurally satisfies `Auditable`.
- [ ] Python: `audit.py` Protocol; basedpyright clean; a test asserts a constructed message satisfies `Auditable` (`isinstance` via `@runtime_checkable`).
- [ ] Hand-written interface files confirmed to survive a `clean: true` regen (they live outside `generated/`).
- [ ] Decide: does this warrant a short Notion ADR (embed-vs-flat convention + per-language thin-interface pattern), or is it adequately covered by ADR-0004 / ADR-0005? Link the decision here.

## Out of scope / follow-ups

* A `derive`/macro to auto-impl the Rust `Auditable` trait for DTOs (manual impls are fine for the first consumers).
* A structured `Actor` message replacing the opaque `created_by` / `modified_by` strings.
* Server-side stamping (who/when is set on write) — that's service-layer behavior, tracked when the first auditable aggregate lands.

## References

* ADR-0004 — Protobuf + buf as single source of truth for wire contracts
* ADR-0005 — Cross-language behavior lives once in `paigasus-kernel`
